theorem geometric-sum
  let a ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  assume a ≠ 1                                                        (H2)
  let n ∈ ℕ₀                                                          (H3)
  then G(n) = (1 − a^(n + 1))/(1 − a)

1.  1 − a ≠ 0
    algebra, from H2
    requires a ∈ ℝ: from H1

2.  G(n) = (1 − a^(n + 1))/(1 − a)
    induction on n starting at 0, from H3

    base
    2.1.  G(0) = 1
          def:G

    2.2.  0 + 1 = 1
          arithmetic

    2.3.  a^(0 + 1) = a^1
          substitute 0 + 1 = 1 (line 2.2)

    2.4.  a^1 = a
          thm:exponent-one a := a, from H1

    2.5.  a^(0 + 1) = a
          calculation
            a^(0 + 1) = a^1       2.3
                      = a         2.4

    2.6.  1 = (1 − a)/(1 − a)
          algebra
          requires 1 − a ≠ 0: from 1
          requires a ∈ ℝ: from H1

    2.7.  (1 − a)/(1 − a) = (1 − a^(0 + 1))/(1 − a)
          substitute a^(0 + 1) = a (line 2.5)

    2.8.  G(0) = (1 − a^(0 + 1))/(1 − a)
          calculation
            G(0) = 1                              2.1
                 = (1 − a)/(1 − a)                2.6
                 = (1 − a^(0 + 1))/(1 − a)        2.7

    step
    2.9.  For every k ∈ ℕ₀, if G(k) = (1 − a^(k + 1))/(1 − a)
          then G(k + 1) = (1 − a^((k + 1) + 1))/(1 − a).
          fix
          let k ∈ ℕ₀                                                  (K)
          assume G(k) = (1 − a^(k + 1))/(1 − a)                       (IH)

          2.9.1.  G(k + 1) = G(k) + a^(k + 1)
                  def:G n := k, from K

          2.9.2.  G(k) + a^(k + 1) = (1 − a^(k + 1))/(1 − a) + a^(k + 1)
                  substitute G(k) = (1 − a^(k + 1))/(1 − a) (IH)

          2.9.3.  k + 1 ∈ ℕ₀
                  thm:nat0-closure, from K

          2.9.4.  a^((k + 1) + 1) = a^(k + 1)·a
                  thm:exponent-step m := k + 1, from H1, 2.9.3

          2.9.5.  (1 − a^(k + 1))/(1 − a) + a^(k + 1) = (1 − a^(k + 1)·a)/(1 − a)
                  algebra
                  requires 1 − a ≠ 0: from 1
                  requires a ∈ ℝ: from H1
                  requires a^(k + 1) ∈ ℝ: thm:power-real m := k + 1, from H1, 2.9.3

          2.9.6.  (1 − a^(k + 1)·a)/(1 − a) = (1 − a^((k + 1) + 1))/(1 − a)
                  substitute a^((k + 1) + 1) = a^(k + 1)·a (line 2.9.4), right to left

          2.9.7.  G(k + 1) = (1 − a^((k + 1) + 1))/(1 − a)
                  calculation
                    G(k + 1) = G(k) + a^(k + 1)                         2.9.1
                             = (1 − a^(k + 1))/(1 − a) + a^(k + 1)      2.9.2
                             = (1 − a^(k + 1)·a)/(1 − a)               2.9.5
                             = (1 − a^((k + 1) + 1))/(1 − a)           2.9.6
